"""claude-bardo: remember every interactive Claude Code session and bring the dead
ones back after a reboot, a terminal crash or a power cut.

  list         what died, what is live (the default; --all adds closed ones, --json for tools)
  restore      relaunch restorable sessions: picker by default, --all, or id prefixes
  resume       relaunch one session in THIS terminal
  forget       mark sessions as closed on purpose (they leave the picker)
  prune        drop old closed/unresumable history
  snapshot     register the sessions that are live right now
  doctor       check the install and every Claude Code internal this depends on
  install      copy to ~/.local/bin and add the hooks (--launchd: picker at login)
  uninstall    remove the hooks, the login agent and the binary (--purge: the registry too)
  hook         SessionStart/SessionEnd hook target (Claude Code pipes JSON on stdin)
  autorestore  login agent target: one window with the picker, only if something died

How "restorable" is decided (measured on Claude Code 2.1.273 to 2.1.285, macOS):
  terminal crash (SIGHUP), reboot (SIGTERM)   SessionEnd "other" / "shutdown"   restorable
  SIGKILL, power loss                         no SessionEnd, <pid>.json lingers  restorable
  /exit, /clear, /resume, /logout, `forget`   a deliberate end                   closed

Registry: $CLAUDE_BARDO_DIR/registry.jsonl (default ~/.local/state/claude-bardo), one JSON
event per line, schema "v": 1. See the README for the schema and the flag replay policy.
"""
